730:
(a) It shall be unlawful for any person to:
(1) Intentionally, and without authority and permission from the owner, injure or destroy any meter, pipe, conduit, wire, pole, lamp, manhole cover, fireplug or any accessories thereto belonging to the city, the utility commission or any other public or private utility (referred to in this section as "owner") engaged in the manufacture, sale or furnishing of electricity, gas, water, telephone, or sanitary sewer services or products, or other public services or products, without the intent to pay the fair cost of repair or replacement thereof;
(2) Intentionally, and without authority and permission from the owner, utilize any such service or consume any such product with the intent not to pay the regular charge for such service or product to the owner, and with the intent to deprive the owner thereof;
(3) Intentionally, and without authority and permission from the owner, prevent a meter from registering the quantity of such service or product supplied, with the intent to deprive the owner of the regular charge for such service or product;
(4) In any way, interfere with the proper action of any such owner, with intent to divert any service or product so as to deprive the owner of the regular charge for such service or product; or
(5) Otherwise, intentionally and without authority, use, or cause to be used, without the consent of such owner, any product or service furnished, manufactured, sold or distributed by such owner, with the intent to deprive the owner of the regular charge for such product or service.
(b) Proof that a person performed any of the acts set forth in subsection (a) of this section, or proof that a person knowingly received the benefits of such acts, or proof that any of the acts specified in subsection (a) of this section were done on the premises in possession of a person, with that person's knowledge, shall be prima facie evidence that such person is responsible for such prohibited acts.
(c) Every person convicted in the municipal court of the city of a violation of any provision of subsection (a) or (b) of this section shall be punished as provided in section 1-12 of this Code.
(Ord. No. 1-2001, 3-15-2001)

738:
The operation and management of the utility systems operated by the city shall be under the utility commission. The utility commission shall have full and plenary power to make all rules and regulations for the management and operation of the utility systems, and to:
(1) Fix, from time to time, the rates charged for water, gas, electricity and other utilities, with the right to classify such rates;
(2) Promulgate and enforce rules and regulations providing for service charges, and the right to classify such charges between resident and nonresident consumers;
(3) Require a reasonable deposit in an amount sufficient to cover estimated consumption from the utility systems;
(4) Make all necessary extensions and do all necessary work for the maintenance and improvement of the utility systems, and make such extensions and improvements, either by letting contracts to the lowest and best bidder, or by doing such work by its own force, as in the judgment of the utility commission, is deemed best; and
(5) Carry on the business of the utility systems.
(Code 1982, § 13-6)
Charter reference— Powers and duties generally, §§ 28, 28A, 33, 33A.

