(a) Required. Every person driving a taxicab in the city must be licensed as a taxicab driver. Before any person shall be entitled to drive any motor vehicle for hire for the transporting of passengers in the city, such person shall first obtain a permit from the chief of police.
(b) Submission of application. All applicants for driver's permits, as required by this article, shall submit an application, in writing, to the chief of police, on a form to be furnished by the police department.
(c) Contents of application. Such application shall be made under oath and shall contain the following:
(1) Age of the applicant;
(2) Applicant's address;
(3) Length of time the applicant has resided in the city;
(4) Applicant's knowledge of the streets and traffic laws of the city;
(5) Applicant's physical infirmities, if any;
(6) Whether the applicant has been convicted of a violation of any applicable section of this Code, laws of the state, the United States or any other state, or any ordinance of the city and, if so, when and of what offense, and the sentence of the court;
(7) Whether the applicant uses alcoholic beverages in any form; and
(8) Applicant's sex and race.
(d) Character references. An applicant for a driver's permit must file with the chief of police, at the time of making such application, affidavits of the applicant's good character from two reputable citizens who have personally known the applicant and observed the applicant's conduct during the year next preceding the date of application.
(Code 1982, § 22-33)
